## How row “text” is computed

There are two distinct text mechanisms:

### A) Inline “card fields” (publication/section/track lines)

In `ScheduleListItemViewModel`, the following properties are *read directly from Fluxor state* via helper:
- `BiblePublicationName`
- `BiblePublicationSectionName`
- `BiblePublicationTrackName`
- Bible-only combined line: `BiblePublicationSectionAndTrackOneLine` (e.g. `"Exodus 9"`)

Helper:
- `ScheduleListItemBibleDisplayNameProvider`
  - file: `src/Bible.Alarm/ViewModels/ScheduleListItemViewModelHelpers/ScheduleListItemBibleDisplayNameProvider.cs`

Notes:
- It treats “Bible” category specially (one-line `"SectionName TrackCode"`).
- If category name is temporarily missing (category isn’t persisted in Schedule DB), it falls back to inferring category from the publication code.

### B) The `SubTitle` + `Language` strings

`ScheduleListItemSubtitleManager` builds `SubTitle` from the `ScheduleStateItem` in Fluxor state:
- it prefers state because display names (section name / track title) are pre-populated during bootstrap and updates
- it intentionally does **not** fall back to DB lookups (Home rendering should not trigger ad-hoc DB work)

File:
- `src/Bible.Alarm/ViewModels/ScheduleListItemViewModelHelpers/ScheduleListItemSubtitleManager.cs`

Subtitle format:
- `Category • Publication • (SectionName if sectioned) • (TrackCode or TrackTitle) • Language`

Track portion rules:
- if sectioned:
  - for **Music category** schedules, it prefers `TrackTitle` if available
  - otherwise it uses the numeric track number
- if non-sectioned:
  - uses track title (dramas/videos)

